>>
Rule 1 (output_size as an integer must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (output_size as a tuple must have exactly two elements)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2
>>
Rule 3 (each element of output_size tuple must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (input must be a 3D or 4D tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 3 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 4
>>
Rule 5 (input must have at least 2 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 6 (input spatial dimensions must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [ndim(v_1) - 2, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
